Error [E-ERR-UNION]: `A | B!` marks only `B` as the error contract.
  --> tests/ui/error_contract_union_needs_parens.jet:11:25
    |
 11 | fn load(id: Int) -> Int SaveError | LoadError! {
    |                         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: The `!` mark follows one type, so a union of error types is grouped for the mark to cover every member.
 Fix: Write `(A | B)!`.
